---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Sidebar from '../../components/Sidebar.astro';
import { buildSchema } from '../../lib/schemas';

const schema = buildSchema.about();
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Dr. Tal Lavian — Telecommunications Expert Witness"
  description="About Dr. Tal Lavian — telecommunications expert witness. Ph.D. UC Berkeley, 120+ patents, 90+ cases, 60+ depositions. Federal court, PTAB & ITC."
  schema={schema}
  ogImage="/images/og/about-dr-lavian.jpg"
>

  <div class="hero-banner">
    <h1>About Dr. Tal Lavian, Ph.D.</h1>
    <div class="hero-stats">
      <div class="hero-stat">
        <div class="hero-stat-number">120+</div>
        <div class="hero-stat-label">Invented Patents</div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-stat">
        <div class="hero-stat-number">60+</div>
        <div class="hero-stat-label">Depositions</div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-stat">
        <div class="hero-stat-number">90+</div>
        <div class="hero-stat-label">Cases</div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-stat">
        <div class="hero-stat-number">25+</div>
        <div class="hero-stat-label">Scientific Publications</div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-stat">
        <div class="hero-stat-number">35+</div>
        <div class="hero-stat-label">Years Experience</div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-stat">
        <div class="hero-stat-number">Ph.D.</div>
        <div class="hero-stat-label">UC Berkeley</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="container">
    <div class="content-with-sidebar">
      <div class="content-main">

        <p class="about-summary">Dr. Tal Lavian is a telecommunications and network communications technologist and technical consultant based in Encino, California. He holds a Ph.D. in Computer Science from UC Berkeley specializing in network communications, an M.Sc. in Electrical Engineering from Tel Aviv University, and a B.Sc. in Mathematics and Computer Science. He is an inventor of 120+ patents and the author of 25+ scientific publications, with nearly 20 years researching, studying, and lecturing at UC Berkeley and more than 35 years of experience in computer networking and telecommunications. He also serves as a <a href="/communications-expert-witness/telecommunications-expert-witness/">telecommunications expert witness</a> in patent litigation.</p>
        <p class="facet-line"><span class="facet-links"><a href="/Dr-Tal-Lavian-CV-Expert-Witness-Network-Communications-Telecommunications-Internet-Protocols-Mobile-Wireless-2026.pdf">Curriculum Vitae (PDF)</a> · <a href="tel:+14082099112">+1 (408) 209-9112</a> · <a href="/contact/">Contact Dr. Lavian</a></span></p>

        <h2>Litigation Record</h2>
        <p>Retained in over <a href="/cases-expert-witness-testimony/">90 cases</a>, with 100+ patents litigated and 60+ depositions. He has filed declarations in more than 90 PTAB proceedings (IPR and CBM).</p>
        <p>Dr. Lavian has testified in U.S. federal courts before judges and juries, the Canadian Federal Court, and a court in Malaysia, and has given declarations and testimony in USPTO Patent Trial and Appeal Board (PTAB) proceedings. He has been retained in International Trade Commission (ITC) Section 337 investigations and in domestic U.S. arbitration proceedings.</p>
        <p>Retained by over 50 <a href="/law-firm-clients/">law firms</a> and <a href="/corporate-clients/">corporate clients</a>, including Fish &amp; Richardson, Kirkland &amp; Ellis, Gibson Dunn, Cooley, and Finnegan. Cases have involved Apple, Google, Microsoft, Cisco, and others. His work spans the <a href="/communications-expert-witness/">technology areas</a> listed on this site.</p>

        <h2>Education and Credentials</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Ph.D., Computer Science, UC Berkeley (network communications)</li>
          <li>M.Sc., Electrical Engineering, Tel Aviv University</li>
          <li>B.Sc., Mathematics and Computer Science</li>
          <li>Industry Fellow and Lecturer, UC Berkeley IEOR Department and SCET</li>
          <li>IEEE Senior Member; ACM member (SIGCOMM, SIGWEB); IEEE-CNSV member</li>
          <li>IEEE-WCET Wireless Communications Engineering Technologies certification (2012)</li>
          <li>Technical Co-Chair, IEEE Hot Interconnects at <a href="https://www.stanford.edu/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Stanford University</a></li>
          <li>Awards: Top Talent Award (Nortel Networks); Top Inventors Award (Nortel EDN); Best Paper Presentation Award (ICE/IEEE Conference)</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Industry Experience</h2>
        <div class="experience-box">
          <img loading="lazy" src="/images/content/globe-communications.jpg" alt="" class="experience-img" width="300" height="300" />
          <p>Principal Scientist, Principal Architect, and Principal Engineer at Nortel Networks&rsquo; Research Labs (1996&ndash;2007; initially Bay Networks, later acquired by Nortel). He led development of a network resource-scheduling service for Grid computing, demonstrated dynamic transatlantic allocation of 10Gbs Lambdas as a grid service, and developed a wire-speed active network on commercial hardware.</p>
          <p>Principal Investigator for three <a href="https://www.darpa.mil/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">DARPA</a> projects in total, including one for the U.S. Air Force Research Lab (<a href="https://www.afrl.af.mil/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">AFRL</a>).</p>
          <p>Other technical positions at Shalev, Scitex, Aptel Communication, Bay Architecture Labs, Ixia, CRadar.Ai, VisuMenu, Aybell, and UC Berkeley. President of the Java Users Group (Mountain View/Silicon Valley), 1999&ndash;2000. Former advisory board member of Quixey, Mytopia, and iLeverage.</p>
        </div>

        <h2>Patents, Publications, and Prosecution</h2>
        <p>Inventor of over 120 <a href="/patents/">patents</a>, with over 60 prosecuted pro se before the USPTO: drafting claims, preparing and filing applications, responding to office actions, and conducting examiner interviews. Co-author of over 25 <a href="/scientific-publications/">scientific publications</a>, journal articles, and peer-reviewed papers, indexed on <a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=DDVtnHEAAAAJ" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Scholar</a>.</p>

        <h2>UC Berkeley and SkyDeck Startups</h2>
        <div class="rd-section">
          <img loading="lazy" src="/images/content/uc-berkeley.png" alt="UC Berkeley" width="300" height="109" class="rd-float-img" />
          <p>Nearly 20 years researching, studying, and lecturing at UC Berkeley. Research projects in data centers (RAD Labs), telecommunication infrastructure (SAHARA), and wireless systems (ICEBERG). Scientific liaison between Nortel Research Lab and UC Berkeley.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="rd-section">
          <img loading="lazy" src="/images/content/cradarai.jpg" alt="CRadar.Ai" width="220" height="98" class="rd-float-img" />
          <p><strong>CRadar.Ai.</strong> CTO and principal investigator of CRadar.Ai, a SkyDeck startup developing a <a href="/ep-3311493-ulpn-frequency-synthesize/">radar</a>-based object detection system for autonomous vehicles.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="rd-section">
          <img loading="lazy" src="/images/content/aybell-logo.png" alt="Aybell" width="150" height="143" class="rd-float-img" />
          <p><strong>Aybell (formerly VisuMenu Inc.).</strong> Co-founder, CEO, and CTO of a SkyDeck startup that turns smartphones into visual menu systems for automated phone menus. He led the design and implementation of its service architecture and voice menu search engine (IVR/PBX using Asterisk, SIP, and VoIP), deployed as a cloud <a href="/communications-expert-witness/pstn-voip-expert-witness/">telecommunications</a> service on Amazon Web Services and Google Cloud Platform.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Credential trust bar (approved figures; one item set sitewide) -->
        <div class="credential-bar" role="group" aria-label="Dr. Lavian's credentials">
        <span class="cred-item"><span class="cred-num">Ph.D.</span> <a href="/about-dr-lavian/">UC Berkeley</a></span>
        <span class="cred-item"><span class="cred-num">120+</span> <a href="/patents/">Invented Patents</a></span>
        <span class="cred-item"><span class="cred-num">100+</span> Patents Litigated</span>
          <span class="cred-item"><span class="cred-num">90+</span> <a href="/cases-expert-witness-testimony/">Cases</a></span>
        <span class="cred-item"><span class="cred-num">60+</span> Depositions</span>
        <span class="cred-item"><span class="cred-num">25+</span> <a href="/scientific-publications/">Publications</a></span>
        <span class="cred-item"><span class="cred-num">35+</span> Years Experience</span>
          <span class="cred-item"><span class="cred-num">50+</span> Law Firms &amp; Corporate Clients</span>
        <div class="cred-companies">Retained by attorneys at Fish &amp; Richardson, Kirkland &amp; Ellis, Gibson Dunn, Finnegan, Irell &amp; Manella, Skadden, and other firms, in cases involving Apple, Google, Microsoft, Cisco, and others.</div>
        </div>

        <section class="faq-section" aria-label="Frequently asked questions about Dr. Tal Lavian">
          <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

          <details open>
            <summary>What are Dr. Lavian&rsquo;s academic credentials?</summary>
            <p>A Ph.D. in Computer Science from UC Berkeley specializing in network communications, an M.Sc. in Electrical Engineering from Tel Aviv University, and a B.Sc. in Mathematics and Computer Science. He is an IEEE Senior Member and an ACM member.</p>
          </details>

          <details>
            <summary>How long was Dr. Lavian at UC Berkeley?</summary>
            <p>Nearly 20 years researching, studying, and lecturing at UC Berkeley, including research projects in data centers (RAD Labs), telecommunication infrastructure (SAHARA), wireless systems (ICEBERG), service as Industry Fellow and Lecturer at the IEOR Department and the Sutardja Center for Entrepreneurship and Technology (SCET), and participation in UC Berkeley&rsquo;s SkyDeck startup accelerator as principal investigator of CRadar.Ai and co-founder, CEO, and CTO of Aybell (formerly VisuMenu Inc.).</p>
          </details>

          <details>
            <summary>How many cases has Dr. Lavian worked on?</summary>
            <p>Over 90 cases, with 100+ patents litigated and 60+ depositions. He has filed declarations in more than 90 PTAB proceedings (IPR and CBM).</p>
          </details>
        </section>

      <aside class="cta-block" aria-label="Contact Dr. Lavian">
        <h2>Contact Dr. Lavian About a Matter</h2>
        <p>To discuss a matter, call <a href="tel:+14082099112">+1 (408) 209-9112</a> or email <!--email_off--><a href="mailto:tlavian@telecommnet.com">tlavian@telecommnet.com</a><!--/email_off-->. Dr. Lavian is based in Encino, California and is available for engagements nationwide.</p>
        <p class="cta-links"><a class="cta-button" href="/contact/">Contact Dr. Lavian</a> <a class="cta-link" href="/Dr-Tal-Lavian-CV-Expert-Witness-Network-Communications-Telecommunications-Internet-Protocols-Mobile-Wireless-2026.pdf">Curriculum Vitae (PDF)</a></p>
      </aside>

      </div>

      <div class="right-col">
        <img src="/images/branding/dr-tal-lavian-portrait-300.webp" srcset="/images/branding/dr-tal-lavian-portrait-300.webp 300w, /images/branding/dr-tal-lavian-portrait-600.webp 600w, /images/branding/dr-tal-lavian-portrait-1200.webp 1200w" sizes="250px" alt="Dr. Tal Lavian, Ph.D." width="250" height="333" loading="eager" class="sidebar-portrait" />
        <Sidebar />
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <style is:global>
    .experience-box {
      background: #f5f5f5;
      padding: 25px;
      margin: 20px 0;
      overflow: hidden;
    }
    .experience-img {
      float: right;
      margin: 0 0 15px 20px;
      max-width: 300px;
    }
    .rd-section {
      overflow: hidden;
    }
    .rd-float-img {
      float: right;
      margin: 0 0 15px 20px;
    }
    @media (max-width: 768px) {
      .experience-img,
      .rd-float-img {
        float: none;
        display: block;
        margin: 0 auto 15px;
      }
    }
  </style>

</BaseLayout>
